  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required for the listener container threading refactor across all three repos, ordered by importance:\n\n**spring-kafka** (primary implementation target):\n- `listener/AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java`, `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java`, `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the core single-threaded \u2192 concurrent container hierarchy\n- `config/AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry.java`, `ContainerCustomizer.java` \u2014 factory/registry wiring that constructs and manages containers\n- `retrytopic/ListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java`, `ListenerContainerFactoryResolver.java` \u2014 dependents that decorate/resolve container factories, at risk of breakage\n- `annotation/KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java` \u2014 endpoint registration path that ties `@KafkaListener` to containers\n- Corresponding test files and `kafka.adoc`/`changes-since-1.0.adoc` docs for behavioral contract and precedent on how threading changes were documented before\n\n**spring-boot** (autoconfiguration/properties consumer):\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java`, `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java`, `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 where concurrency would be exposed as a configurable property and wired into the container factory bean\n- Corresponding test files\n\n**spring-framework** (core abstractions):\n- `context/SmartLifecycle.java` \u2014 lifecycle contract the containers implement (start/stop/phase semantics matter for concurrent sub-containers)\n- `core/task/TaskExecutor.java` \u2014 the executor abstraction underlying concurrent listener thread management",
